ui/gtk: Screen off cover and Wake from the guest display power

The ASoftware kernel lights its virtio keyboard's Scroll Lock LED while
iOS has the display off (xnu 0102) and keeps the last frame on screen.
With sidebar=on a dark "Screen off" cover now lies over the guest display
then (a click on it presses the side button, F2), and the Lock button
reads Wake. The display power arrives through the LED notifier, on the
vCPU thread, and is shown from an idle callback. iOS turns the display
off once while it boots, under the Apple logo, so the cover is armed only
after the display was on again after that.
Based on QEMU v11.1.2 with 0002-0006.

